Upstream credits, preserved here because parts of the vendored core derive
from them:

- VCC (View-oriented Conversation Compiler) by lllyasviel
  https://github.com/lllyasviel/VCC — the original transcript-preserving
  conversation compiler that inspired pi-vcc.
- pi-blackhole by k0valik
  https://github.com/k0valik/pi-blackhole — recall `mode:"touched"`,
  `#N:path` drill-down, and the session-global `#N` counting rule
  (src/core/global-indices.ts, ported from pi-blackhole commit f82e07a).
- monotykamary/pi-vcc (`tom` branch)
  https://github.com/monotykamary/pi-vcc — the invisible auto-continue
  pattern, which this port does not include (dsh owns run continuation).

